  "decision": "map_front",

  "rationale": "Round 2 left the front well-populated on the accuracy axis (10.0 to 21.4 bits, i.e. essentially the full feasible span) but only 13 designs, and the high-accuracy end stops at 21.4 bits / area 12998 while the registry still allows data_width up to 28 and n_iter up to 30 — so the right-hand (high-accuracy) part of the trade-off curve is under-sampled and there is clear hypervolume left against the (40000, 10) reference. The low-area end is also pinned right against the constraint boundary (best design area 7349 at accuracy 10.02 bits, max_abs_err 0.000965 vs limit 0.000976562), so the exact minimum-area feasible corner is fragile and worth re-mapping. Both families found on the front (iterative, unrolled_k) should be swept over their full ranges seeded with the current front, which is exactly the reserved mapping step. With 80 of 200 evals still available and 2 rounds left, spending this round on a seeded NSGA-II front map is the highest-value use of budget before any final refinement.",

  "next_plan": null

}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "next_plan": null,
  "rationale": "Budget is exhausted (200/200 evals) and this is the capped final round, so the choice is between `stop` and `infeasible`. It is not infeasible: 159/200 evaluations are feasible, 140 unique, and neither constraint is binding at the front — 0% of evaluations violate throughput_msps >= 1 (best seen 13 MSPS) and only 20% violate the error bound, with best seen max_abs_err 8.91e-08 (2^-23.42). The feasible Pareto front spans area_um2 7349..14983 against the HV reference 40000 and accuracy_bits 10..23.4 against reference 10, i.e. the objective range is well covered, and hypervolume is still gaining (+16.0% this round, HV 3.898e+05), from an already dense front of 21 designs. The selection rule (min area_um2) is satisfied by a design on the front: iterative [data_width=16 n_iter=23 angle_guard=0 frac_guard=0 rounding=trunc] at area_um2=7349, ffs=105, throughput_msps=5.44, max_abs_err=0.000965 (2^-10.02) — inside the 2^-10 error budget with ~1.2% margin and 5.4x the required 1 MSPS. Both explored families contribute (iterative best area 7349; unrolled_k best 9127, best accuracy 16.88 bits), so there is no unexplored family that could plausibly push the low-area corner below the current front — and the full-range mapping pass for the families on the front was already spent within the budget. Further rounds would only refine accuracy on the already-covered high-accuracy tail, which the area-minimising selection rule does not pick. Stop here; the front is the deliverable and the min-area point meets the spec."
